Fallback Crypto chooses which of the kernel's crypto drivers encrypts
the IPsec tunnels the host carries itself - on a Sophos XGS, those its
coprocessor does not take: aesni, as OPNsense ships, or ossl, the
kernel's OpenSSL-based driver, beside aesni or in its place. The page
shows the host's processor and the features AES-GCM depends on, the
crypto providers present, and the IPsec SAs the host holds with their
algorithms.

